{title: 619 - Lead On, O King Eternal}
{artist: Seventh-day Adventist Hymnal}
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: C}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{tag: Christian Life}
{tag: }

Verse 1:
[C]Lead on, O [F]King E[C]ternal,
[C7]The [F]day of [C]march [F]has [G]come;
[G7]Hence[C]forth [C7]in [F]fields of [C]conquest
Thy [G]tents shall [D7]be our [G]home.
[G7]Through [C]days [C7]of prepa[F]ration
[A7]Thy [D]grace [D7]has made us [G]strong;
[G7]And [C]now, O [Dm7]King [C7]e[F]ternal,
We [C]lift our [G7]battle [C]song.

Verse 2:
[C]Lead [F]on, O [C]King eternal,
[C7]till [F]sin's [C]fierce [F]war [G]shall cease,
[G7][C]and [C7]holiness [F]shall [C]whisper
[G]the [D7]sweet amen [G]of peace.
[G7]For [C]not with [C7]swords [F]loud clashing,
[A7]nor [D]roll [D7]of [G]stirring drums;
[G7]with [C]deeds [Dm7]of [C7]love [F]and mercy
[C]the [G7]heavenly [C]kingdom comes.

Verse 3:
[C]Lead [F]on, O [C]King eternal,
[C7]we [F]follow, [C]not [F]with [G]fears,
[G7]for [C]gladness [C7]breaks [F]like [C]morning
[G]where'er [D7]thy [G]face appears.
[G7]Thy [C]cross is [C7]lifted [F]o'er us,
[A7]we [D]journey [D7]in [G]its light;
[G7]the [C]crown [Dm7]awaits [C7]the [F]conquest;
[C]lead on, [G7]O God [C]of might.
